I'll kill you!

210
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:41,505
Frannie, we need to make
some kind of rope.

211
00:10:41,574 --> 00:10:44,209
Perhaps out of curtains.

212
00:10:44,277 --> 00:10:46,117
I couldn't get the window shut.

213
00:10:46,162 --> 00:10:47,328
The water's rising!

214
00:10:47,397 --> 00:10:49,208
I'll get us out of this.

215
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:54,335
I'm not gonna make it, babe.

216
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:57,071
I-I want you
to take my Hacky Sack...

217
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:59,607
and-and give it
to our grandchildren.

218
00:10:59,675 --> 00:11:01,220
Jeff, we don't even have kids.

219
00:11:01,244 --> 00:11:02,744
I know.

220
00:11:02,812 --> 00:11:06,547
That's why I want you to take
this folded-up candy wrapper.

221
00:11:06,616 --> 00:11:08,349
Don't ask me how I did it.

222
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:11,386
Just take it
and start our family.

223
00:11:11,455 --> 00:11:15,590
It looks like this corridor
should take us directly
to the main attic access.

224
00:11:15,659 --> 00:11:18,159
It's not a corridor.
It's a hallway.

225
00:11:18,227 --> 00:11:20,428
You need to stop
with the architect jargon.

226
00:11:20,497 --> 00:11:22,330
Seriously. Look at me.

227
00:11:22,398 --> 00:11:26,033
You need to zip it, lock it
and put it in your pocket.

228
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:27,435
Stan?

229
00:11:27,504 --> 00:11:30,049
It's Mom!
She's gonna save us!

230
00:11:30,073 --> 00:11:32,574
We don't need saving.
I've got this under control.

231
00:11:32,642 --> 00:11:34,409
I'm here, Francine!
Don't panic.

232
00:11:34,478 --> 00:11:36,144
I'll get us through this.

233
00:11:36,213 --> 00:11:40,615
What?
Stan, we're moving
the stuff off the door.

234
00:11:40,683 --> 00:11:42,917
Just hang on.
That's real good, honey.

235
00:11:42,986 --> 00:11:45,120
Keep your spirits up.
I'm coming.

236
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:49,974
There, there.
You're safe now.

237
00:11:52,895 --> 00:11:54,890
The wigs!
They're all gone.

238
00:11:54,914 --> 00:11:57,782
Half of those belonged
to Brendan Fraser.

239
00:11:58,685 --> 00:12:00,779
Oh, thank the stars you made it.

240
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:02,147
Come here.
I've got you.

241
00:12:02,171 --> 00:12:04,772
Oh, bless you, Roger.
I was afraid I...

242
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:07,275
Thank God this one survived.

243
00:12:07,343 --> 00:12:09,624
I can still go
to cowboy weddings.

244
00:12:09,679 --> 00:12:11,612
<i>Nein! Nein!</i>

245
00:12:14,183 --> 00:12:15,849
Okay, one at a time.

246
00:12:15,918 --> 00:12:18,369
The rope isn't very strong.

247
00:12:18,438 --> 00:12:20,450
Aaah! I don't want
to die here.

248
00:12:20,474 --> 00:12:23,958
I'm supposed to die
in the medical tent
at a music festival.

249
00:12:25,495 --> 00:12:27,228
Jeff, no!

250
00:12:27,297 --> 00:12:29,730
Ow!
Jeff!
Now we lost our rope.

251
00:12:29,799 --> 00:12:31,883
I'm so sorry.

252
00:12:31,951 --> 00:12:33,918
Get ahold of yourself.

253
00:12:38,107 --> 00:12:39,290
Huh.

254
00:12:41,811 --> 00:12:43,161
Huh.

255
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:45,624
How are we gonna
get up there now?

256
00:12:45,648 --> 00:12:47,359
Get us outta here,
Mrs. S.

257
00:12:47,383 --> 00:12:48,883
No! I'll save us.

258
00:12:48,951 --> 00:12:51,085
We, uh...
We should open a window...

259
00:12:51,154 --> 00:12:52,653
and flood this floor.

260
00:12:52,722 --> 00:12:55,239
The rising water will carry us
right up to the living room.

261
00:12:55,308 --> 00:12:58,626
There's no way
we're doing another one
of your ideas, Stan.

262
00:13:01,214 --> 00:13:03,064
Maybe we should.

263
00:13:03,132 --> 00:13:06,568
What?
Look, I know Dad's decisions
haven't worked out,

264
00:13:06,636 --> 00:13:08,135
but he<i> is</i> trying.

265
00:13:08,204 --> 00:13:10,905
I say we open the window.

266
00:13:10,973 --> 00:13:13,775
Unless anyone has a better idea.

267
00:13:13,843 --> 00:13:16,010
Based in reality.

268
00:13:16,078 --> 00:13:17,762
Okay then.
Window it is.

269
00:13:17,830 --> 00:13:20,214
- Thank you, Hayley.
- You're welcome, Dad.

270
00:13:26,589 --> 00:13:30,191
Dad was wrong!

271
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:32,927
Wow. What a beautiful creature.

272
00:13:32,995 --> 00:13:34,915
And we know so little
about them.

273
00:13:40,870 --> 00:13:42,053
Hayley!
Hayley!

274
00:13:42,121 --> 00:13:43,287
Oh, God! Oh, God!

275
00:13:43,356 --> 00:13:44,996
That shark's in here, man.

276
00:13:45,058 --> 00:13:47,339
If they're really
attracted to blood,
then it's in my room,

277
00:13:47,393 --> 00:13:51,129
attacking the boxers I wore
the day Francine made tacos.

278
00:13:51,198 --> 00:13:53,064
Just leave me behind.

279
00:13:53,133 --> 00:13:56,234
I<i> am</i> bad in a crisis,
and it got Hayley killed.

280
00:13:56,303 --> 00:13:59,820
Don't give up, Dad.
We got the window closed,
and we'll find her.

281
00:14:02,441 --> 00:14:05,176
It's the ghost
of Hayley, risen up
from the depths of hell.

282
00:14:05,245 --> 00:14:07,011
She has unfinished business
with me.

283
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:10,348
Leave me be, specter!
No, she's alive.

284
00:14:10,416 --> 00:14:12,856
Why would you assume
she went to hell?

285
00:14:13,486 --> 00:14:15,336
Hayley!

286
00:14:15,405 --> 00:14:18,089
What's on the bottom
of your mattress, Steve?

287
00:14:18,157 --> 00:14:20,358
So many of the girls are Asian.

288
00:14:20,426 --> 00:14:21,926
And pregnant.

289
00:14:21,995 --> 00:14:23,595
She's not in here.
We should keep moving.

290
00:14:26,799 --> 00:14:29,517
Shark!
Oh, thank God.
It's just a dead girl.

291
00:14:29,585 --> 00:14:33,320
Aaah!
Roger. You came back for me.

292
00:14:33,389 --> 00:14:34,889
Uh, okay.

293
00:14:34,958 --> 00:14:39,360
Do you want to come to dinner
at my parents' house on Tuesday?

294
00:14:39,429 --> 00:14:41,779
What did you find?
I-Is it Hayley?

295
00:14:41,847 --> 00:14:43,847
No, it's nothing.
Just a cushion.

296
00:14:45,118 --> 00:14:47,985
We're gonna have lots of babies.

297
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:50,704
No, no, no, no, no, no.

298
00:14:51,791 --> 00:14:53,791
She's not in here either.

299
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:56,628
Where's your father?
The shark got him!

300
00:14:56,696 --> 00:14:59,346
Stan! Hayley!

301
00:14:59,415 --> 00:15:01,775
I don't see any...

302
00:15:02,134 --> 00:15:04,652
- Hayley!
- Careful.

303
00:15:04,721 --> 00:15:07,655
The shark let me go
when I jammed my one-hitter
in its eye,

304
00:15:07,724 --> 00:15:10,057
but I think
it's still here somewhere.

305
00:15:19,502 --> 00:15:22,136
Hang on, Hayley!
Mama's coming!

306
00:15:27,927 --> 00:15:30,328
Does anyone have ChapStick?

307
00:15:32,081 --> 00:15:34,381
I gotcha, honey.
It's okay...

308
00:15:36,319 --> 00:15:38,102
Go, go, go!

309
00:15:43,259 --> 00:15:44,825
We have to go up.

310
00:15:45,678 --> 00:15:46,777
Oh!

311
00:15:51,868 --> 00:15:54,469
We did it.

312
00:15:54,537 --> 00:15:56,754
We got away.

313
00:15:56,823 --> 00:15:58,890
Okay, according
to the blueprints...

314
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,274
Aaah!

315
00:16:00,343 --> 00:16:03,077
It's hungry for flesh
<i>and</i> knowledge.

316
00:16:03,162 --> 00:16:04,996
Aaah!

317
00:16:07,316 --> 00:16:08,916
Don't look at me, whore.

318
00:16:08,984 --> 00:16:10,717
We both know what this is.

319
00:16:10,786 --> 00:16:13,187
It's love. Forever love.

320
00:16:17,576 --> 00:16:19,493
Stan!

321
00:16:19,562 --> 00:16:21,061
I didn't see you there.

322
00:16:21,130 --> 00:16:22,496
S-S-Sneaky.

323
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:25,165
A sneaky boy is what you are.

324
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:27,802
Francine was right
about me, Klaus.

325
00:16:27,870 --> 00:16:30,871
The farther away
from the family I am,
the safer they'll be.

326
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:33,385
- There he is! There he is!
- Look at all his teeth!

327
00:16:33,409 --> 00:16:36,376
They don't sound
very safe, Stan.
You'd better get in there.

328
00:16:36,446 --> 00:16:40,464
I want to,
but I'll only make things worse
with my bad decisions.

329
00:16:40,533 --> 00:16:42,845
Look, Stan, everyone
makes bad decisions,

330
00:16:42,869 --> 00:16:44,646
but it's a numbers game.

331
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:48,100
Eventually, you're bound
to make the right call.

332
00:16:48,124 --> 00:16:49,974
- I am?
- Sure.

333
00:16:50,043 --> 00:16:53,844
Look at Nicolas Cage.
He made many horrible movies.

334
00:16:53,913 --> 00:16:56,914
<i>Snake Eyes, 8MM,
Gone in Sixty Seconds,</i>

335
00:16:56,983 --> 00:16:59,150
<i>Captain Corelli's Mandolin,
Windtalkers...</i>

336
00:16:59,218 --> 00:17:02,953
<i>Ghost Rider, Family Man,
Weather Man, Wicker Man,</i>

337
00:17:03,022 --> 00:17:05,300
<i>- Bangkok Dangerous...</i>
- Look! There's his fin!

338
00:17:05,324 --> 00:17:07,424
But then he nailed it, Stan,

339
00:17:07,493 --> 00:17:09,293
with<i> National Treasure 2,</i>

340
00:17:09,361 --> 00:17:11,929
the greatest movie of all time!

341
00:17:11,998 --> 00:17:13,781
He<i> did</i> nail it.

342
00:17:13,850 --> 00:17:19,286
He nailed it so hard
that he<i> became</i>
a national treasure... too.

343
00:17:19,355 --> 00:17:21,032
Mom, behind you!

344
00:17:21,056 --> 00:17:22,790
My God.

345
00:17:22,859 --> 00:17:27,260
If Nicolas Cage can recover
from his bad decisions
and make a great one, so can I.

346
00:17:27,329 --> 00:17:28,846
That's the spirit.

347
00:17:28,914 --> 00:17:31,832
I'm going to save my family.

348
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:37,004
This time, I'm going
to make the right call.

349
00:17:37,873 --> 00:17:39,718
I don't want to die yet.

350
00:17:39,742 --> 00:17:41,742
I haven't experienced
the disappointment...

351
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:44,145
of being in a monogamous
sexual relationship.

352
00:17:44,213 --> 00:17:46,947
- Aaah!
- Help has arrived.

353
00:17:49,168 --> 00:17:51,814
It's okay.
I let the bear in
to kill the shark.

354
00:17:51,838 --> 00:17:54,588
They're natural enemies
since the dawn of time.

355
00:17:59,946 --> 00:18:01,578
They're working in tandem.

356
00:18:01,647 --> 00:18:04,047
They're brothers in arms.

357
00:18:05,702 --> 00:18:08,936
Just a hiccup. Don't worry.
I'm Nick Caging this mother.

358
00:18:11,373 --> 00:18:13,741
This time
I'll make the right call.

359
00:18:13,809 --> 00:18:16,110
I'm gonna electrocute 'em.

360
00:18:16,179 --> 00:18:18,078
Oh, Stan, I don't think...

361
00:18:19,466 --> 00:18:21,098
Aaah!

362
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:35,763
Don't worry. I'm on this.
Next time, I'm bound
to make the right call.

363
00:18:35,831 --> 00:18:38,399
You're killing us, Mr. S.
Stop it!

364
00:18:38,467 --> 00:18:40,834
Stay calm, Jeff.
I'll get us through this.

365
00:18:40,904 --> 00:18:43,249
You have to let... me...
help... you.

366
00:18:43,273 --> 00:18:44,772
Stan!

367
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:47,191
I know, honey.
You believe in me again.

368
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:50,845
No! You're making
everything much, much worse.

369
00:18:50,914 --> 00:18:52,479
Now look me in the eyes.

370
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:56,200
I'm going to tell you
exactly what to do.

371
00:18:56,252 --> 00:18:58,986
You need to go out and get help.

372
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:01,655
No more decisions or ideas.

373
00:19:01,724 --> 00:19:05,343
Go outside and get help. Okay?

374
00:19:05,411 --> 00:19:08,095
Okay. I hear you.
I really do.

375
00:19:08,163 --> 00:19:11,999
But I'm not going to do that,
because I have a better idea:

376
00:19:12,067 --> 00:19:15,452
my old college javelin.

377
00:19:15,521 --> 00:19:17,004
Remember?

378
00:19:18,007 --> 00:19:19,590
I'll harpoon the bear,

379
00:19:19,658 --> 00:19:22,320
and the bear blood
will distract the shark,
and we can escape.

380
00:19:22,344 --> 00:19:24,195
Stan!

381
00:19:31,888 --> 00:19:33,687
No!

382
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:43,080
Aaah!

383
00:19:51,357 --> 00:19:53,157
Sorry about
tranquilizing you, Stan.

384
00:19:53,225 --> 00:19:56,326
I-I wasn't sure who was doing
the most damage down there.

385
00:19:56,395 --> 00:19:57,862
It's okay.

386
00:19:57,931 --> 00:19:59,997
You did the right thing, Buckle.

387
00:20:00,066 --> 00:20:02,233
You harpooned me.

388
00:20:02,301 --> 00:20:05,218
I told you
to go out and get help,

389
00:20:05,288 --> 00:20:07,421
and you harpooned me.

390
00:20:07,490 --> 00:20:09,940
I'm so sorry, Francine.

391
00:20:10,008 --> 00:20:13,794
I just wanted to prove
I'm good in a crisis.
I failed.

392
00:20:13,863 --> 00:20:18,765
Stan, 99% of the time
there is no crisis,

393
00:20:18,835 --> 00:20:22,102
and you're a wonderful
husband and father.

394
00:20:22,171 --> 00:20:23,949
But what about
when there is one?

395
00:20:23,973 --> 00:20:26,273
It's the man's job
to protect his family.

396
00:20:26,342 --> 00:20:28,342
And you can, honey.

397
00:20:28,410 --> 00:20:31,445
By getting the hell out
of the way and doing nothing.

398
00:20:31,514 --> 00:20:34,248
Huh. Do nothing.

399
00:20:35,785 --> 00:20:39,303
Francine, we both know
I'm not going to do that.

400
00:20:39,372 --> 00:20:42,890
I wonder how much damage
the hurricane did
to the neighborhood.

401
00:20:48,464 --> 00:20:51,131
- Oh, what a day.
- Tell me about it.

402
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:53,133
I don't even know
where the hell I am.

403
00:20:53,202 --> 00:20:55,235
Looter!
Self-defense!

404
00:20:55,304 --> 00:20:58,344
A black and a white talking
as if it's normal.

405
00:20:59,608 --> 00:21:02,410
Peter, what are you doin'?
You know me.

406
00:21:02,478 --> 00:21:04,823
Everybody shut up
and let me think.
Just let me think!

407
00:21:04,847 --> 00:21:07,080
Stan, have you...

408
00:21:09,886 --> 00:21:12,887
Oh, man.
Classic<i> American Dad!</i>

409
00:21:45,504 --> 00:21:47,437
Bye! Have a beautiful time.